TopoForge -- installation

There is nothing to install.  TopoForge is one HTML file, index.html.  Open it
in a web browser (double-click it, or drag it onto a browser window).  It runs
from file://, offline, with no server and no network calls.  Your work is
saved in that browser; use File > Export to keep copies elsewhere.

Check a copy
------------
Every file in a release is listed in SHA256SUMS.  From the folder holding it:

    sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS            # GNU coreutils; each line should say OK
    shasum -a 256 -c SHA256SUMS        # the same, where sha256sum is missing

Bryant's version 1.5 has this sha256:

    6a76e9ca66e6a2733a35677c11599114b4009529568580526d90427fa08a9e2a

so a single file can be checked by hand:

    sha256sum upstream/topoforge-1.5.html

A signed release also carries a detached signature by Corwin Brust:

    gpg --verify topoforge-VERSION.tar.gz.asc topoforge-VERSION.tar.gz

His key's fingerprint is

    ECE7 7CF4 17C7 6C1A CFCE  7C2B 5B61 3551 1580 F007

(no signed release yet, as of 2026-10-08).

The scripts
-----------
From a source tree (POSIX sh; run each with sh, since a copy may have no
execute bit):

    sh bin/verify.sh       is upstream/ still v1.5; do files match SHA256SUMS
    sh bin/test.sh         every test kit (TopoForge's own need jq; the
                           project-files kit needs python3)
    sh bin/sums.sh         write SHA256SUMS
    sh bin/ship.sh 1.6     verify, test, sum, pack dist/topoforge-1.6.tar.gz
                           (GNU tar, for --transform)
    sh bin/tangle.sh       remake bin/ from RECIPE.org (or C-c C-v t in Emacs)

